/* =====================================================================
   AVB1 "VIDBuddy" — Audio/Video Buddy handheld monitor (Ward-Beck Systems, 2002|35 – 2007|40).
   Plugin for the WBS Device Simulator. (Not Audio Video Bridging: see rd79-avb-monitor.js.)

   How this model works
   --------------------
   The unit has three PIC16F874s (AVB1-2ISS3.bom): U200 on the front board (buttons, lamps, LCD power,
   battery and charging), U201 next to it (the 2 x 17 LED meter) and U4 on the main board (CS8415 AES
   receiver, GS9023 embedded-audio demux, ADV7171 encoder, power switching). The plugin carries the
   archived MPASM sources verbatim (U200 v1.04, U201 v1.00, AVB1-1 v1.04 — the 16F874 builds), assembles
   them with the project options /c- /rdec, and runs all three cores in lock-step at 4.9152 MHz
   (813.8 ns per instruction cycle), wired as in avb1-2iss3.net: the 9600 Bd link between U200 and U4,
   CAL and the shared oscillator to U201, the bit-banged SPI/parallel/I2C buses to the U4 peripherals,
   the relays and the peak detectors. Every timing on the timeline comes out of that run.

   Sources (archive folder "#AV #SERIES/XXX- AVB  VID BUDDY - #OBSOLETE #Archive"):
   - AVB - #Software/... (three firmware trees, all versions; .pjt/.mcp/.err)
   - AVB - #PCB/avb1-2iss3.net, AVB1-2ISS3.bom, .pnp, .ECO (P-CAD 2002, ISSUE 3, 2006|39)
   - AVB - #SILK/avb1-frontssv1.cdr, avb1-sidessv2curve.cdr, avb1-REARssv3curve.cdr (+ ssv1/ssv2/ssv3temp)
     converted with Inkscape; ink layers cut to assets/avb-vid-buddy-front-ink.png, -side-ink.png,
     -rear-ink.png; text re-set in SVG at the CorelDRAW positions (libcdr loses text alignment)
   - AVBManual.doc (2002|35), AVB1Manual Page6.cdr, AVB1MANU.cdr, AVBControls.pdf (2004|37)
   - AVB - #MECHANICAL/AVB1-M1…M12 (panel size, paint "EXTRA FINE TEXTURED WBS BLACK")
   Anything not in those files is marked "inferred" on screen.
   ===================================================================== */
